  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math> are in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>GP</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>b</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>c</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>c</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;are in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AP</mi></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>c</mi></math> are the lengths of the sides of a triangle, which is",
    "image": null
